## Subject-level drift rates and thresholds

To visualize the individual variability of our parameters of interest, distributions of the means of the subject-level posterior distributions for threshold (Learned and Novel) and drift rate (Learned and Novel) can be found in @fig-ind-param.











::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Distribution of subject-level posterior means of the threshold parameter (Learned and Novel) and the drift rate parameter (Learned and Novel). Black doted lines denotate the median parameter estimates and the small color lines denotate the individual subject mean parameter estimates.](supplementary_files/figure-typst/fig-ind-param-1.png){#fig-ind-param}
:::
:::


To assess whether participants' parameter estimates varied enough to support an individual-differences approach, we compared the spread of the subject-level posterior means with the precision of each individual estimate. Estimates from hierarchical models are shrunk toward the group mean, so their observed spread understates true between-participant variance. More importantly, variability is only meaningful when it exceeds the uncertainty of each estimate [@haines2025tutorial; @hedge2018reliability; @rouder2019psychometrics]. For each parameter and condition, we therefore computed the ratio of the between-participant SD of posterior means to the average within-participant posterior SD. Ratios were [1.88–2.04] for threshold and [1.307–1.535] for drift rate, indicating that participants differed by more than the uncertainty in their individual estimates. As a complementary check, we computed, for each participant, the 95% credible interval of their deviation from the group-level estimate. For threshold, 28.3% (learned) and 29.7% (novel) of participants deviated credibly from the group mean; for drift rate, the proportions were 11.0% (learned) and 18.3% (novel). All proportions exceed the maximum of 5% expected if participants did not differ, which is a conservative benchmark given hierarchical shrinkage. Together, these results indicate substantial between-participant variability.


::: {#tbl-diagnostics .cell tbl-cap='Between-Participant Variability in Subject-Level LBA Parameter Estimates Relative to Estimation Uncertainty' tbl-height='10' tbl-width='15'}
::: {.cell-output-display}

