Point estimates correlations with recognition scores. In (b), drift rate (TRUE) reflects the accumulation of evidence when the response is correct and drift rate (FALSE) the accumulation of evidence when the response is incorrect. Drift rate (TRUE-FALSE) represent the signal-to-noise ratio provided by the stimulus.
:::


