## Bayesian linear regression models for threshold parameter

We ran two Bayesian linear regression models to estimate if face recognition ability could predict the threshold parameter (response cautions) for both the Learned and Novel responses. The models description can be found in @tbl-regression-model-tresh-formula. 

Following our preregistration, the predictions of the two regression models for threshold can be seen in @fig-prediction-thresh.
From visual inspection, the response caution seems to increase when face recognition increases for both the Learned and Novel response.
This pattern of prediction remains the same when accounting for car recognition ability for the "Learned" response but not for the "Novel" response.
Inspection of the posterior predictions in @tbl-pred-acc-thresh shows that some of these predicted intervals overlap with 0, and that caution is needed when extrapolating these results.

